---
title: Din Tai Fung Cucumber Salad
source: https://platingsandpairings.com/din-tai-fung-cucumber-salad-recipe
prep time: 4 hours
servings: 3
tags: asian cucumber salad, cucumber salad, din tai fung
course: Salad
cuisine: Asian
---

Add @persian cucumbers{8}(sliced into 1/2-inch thick pieces. Can substitute with 2 english cucumbers per 8 persian) to a small bowl.

Sprinkle with @kosher salt{1½%tbsp} and toss to combine. Let sit for ~{30%minutes} in the refrigerator.

After ~{30%minutes}, rinse off the salt mixture and pat the cucumbers dry.

Meanwhile, make the dressing. In a small bowl, whisk together @rice vinegar{3%tbsp}, @mirin{1½%tbsp}, @sugar{2%tbsp}, @sesame oil{1½%tbsp}, @garlic{3%cloves}(grated or minced, about 1tbsp for 3 cloves), and @kosher salt{½%teaspoon}. Mix well and set aside.

Toss the rinsed and dried cucumbers with the dressing and let marinate for a minimum of ~{4%hours}, up to ~{2%days}.

To serve: Taste for seasoning, and add additional @kosher salt{} if needed. Drizzle with @chili oil{1/2%tbsp}(or more, to taste) and sprinkle with @fresno chile pepper{1}(minced)(optional) and serve chilled.